@page "/technology"
<PageTitle>Technology stack | CompileCare</PageTitle>
<main class="page-shell">
    <section class="page-hero tech-hero"><div class="container"><span class="section-kicker">ENGINEERING & TECHNOLOGY</span><h1>The technology behind <span>CompileCare.</span></h1><p>A transparent, repository-derived view of the frameworks, libraries, data platforms, infrastructure and engineering tools used across the platform. Versions shown are those declared in the current project configuration and may evolve.</p><div class="tech-summary"><span><b>.NET</b> core platform</span><span><b>PostgreSQL</b> transactional data</span><span><b>React + TypeScript</b> hospital workspace</span><span><b>OpenTelemetry</b> observability</span></div></div></section>
    <section class="section compact-section"><div class="container">
        <div class="notice"><b>Scope and version notes</b><p>This catalogue covers the current repositories and their checked-in configurations. The API targets .NET 10; the public information website currently targets .NET 8; shared observability packages target .NET 9 and are consumed by the API. PostgreSQL 17 is configured for the local development stack and PostgreSQL 16 for the API integration-test stack. Redis is an optional integration in the shared caching package, not a mandatory dependency of the core API. Planned integrations are identified separately from technologies currently configured.</p></div>
        <div class="tech-group"><div class="tech-group-heading"><span class="section-kicker">01 / APPLICATION DEVELOPMENT</span><h2>Languages, frameworks & user experiences</h2><p>Separate applications serve the public information site and the authenticated hospital workspace.</p></div><div class="tech-grid">
            <article class="tech-card"><img src="https://cdn.simpleicons.org/dotnet/512BD4" alt=".NET logo"/><div><h3>.NET 10 / C#</h3><p>Primary backend and shared-library platform. API, Application, Infrastructure, API Client and Caching projects target .NET 10.</p><small>Backend · SDK 10.0.100</small></div></article>
            <article class="tech-card"><img src="https://cdn.simpleicons.org/dotnet/512BD4" alt="ASP.NET Core logo"/><div><h3>ASP.NET Core</h3><p>HTTP API host, minimal endpoints, middleware, dependency injection, authentication, health endpoints and the public site hosting runtime.</p><small>API · Public site</small></div></article>
            <article class="tech-card"><img src="https://cdn.simpleicons.org/csharp/512BD4" alt="C sharp logo"/><div><h3>C#</h3><p>Application contracts, domain workflows, infrastructure adapters, integration clients and automated backend tests.</p><small>Primary backend language</small></div></article>
            <article class="tech-card"><img src="https://cdn.simpleicons.org/react/61DAFB" alt="React logo"/><div><h3>React 19</h3><p>Component-based authenticated hospital workspace, with permission-aware module navigation and responsive workflows.</p><small>Authenticated Web</small></div></article>
            <article class="tech-card"><img src="https://cdn.simpleicons.org/typescript/3178C6" alt="TypeScript logo"/><div><h3>TypeScript 5.9</h3><p>Typed browser application code, API integration, UI state and test suites.</p><small>Authenticated Web</small></div></article>
            <article class="tech-card"><img src="https://cdn.simpleicons.org/vite/646CFF" alt="Vite logo"/><div><h3>Vite 7</h3><p>Frontend development server and production build pipeline for the React application.</p><small>Frontend tooling</small></div></article>
            <article class="tech-card"><img src="https://cdn.simpleicons.org/react/61DAFB" alt="React Router logo"/><div><h3>React Router 7</h3><p>Client-side navigation and route composition in the authenticated Web application.</p><small>Frontend routing</small></div></article>
            <article class="tech-card"><img src="https://cdn.simpleicons.org/dotnet/512BD4" alt="Blazor logo"/><div><h3>Blazor Server</h3><p>Server-interactive Razor component model used by the separate public CompileCare.Site project.</p><small>Public site · .NET 8</small></div></article>
            <article class="tech-card"><img src="https://cdn.simpleicons.org/dotnet/512BD4" alt="MudBlazor logo"/><div><h3>MudBlazor 8.14</h3><p>Component library configured in the public Blazor website for layout and UI components.</p><small>Public site</small></div></article>
            <article class="tech-card"><img src="https://cdn.simpleicons.org/bootstrap/7952B3" alt="Bootstrap logo"/><div><h3>Bootstrap 5.3</h3><p>Responsive CSS framework loaded by the public website alongside its custom design system.</p><small>Public site styling</small></div></article>
            <article class="tech-card"><img src="https://cdn.simpleicons.org/nodedotjs/5FA04E" alt="Node.js logo"/><div><h3>Node.js 22</h3><p>Build-stage runtime used to install frontend dependencies and compile the React application image.</p><small>Frontend container build</small></div></article>
            <article class="tech-card"><img src="https://cdn.simpleicons.org/keycloak/4D4D4D" alt="OpenID Connect logo"/><div><h3>oidc-client-ts 3.3</h3><p>Browser OIDC client supporting Authorization Code with PKCE, callback handling and session renewal flows.</p><small>Authenticated Web</small></div></article>
        </div></div>
        <div class="tech-group"><div class="tech-group-heading"><span class="section-kicker">02 / DATA & PERSISTENCE</span><h2>Transactional storage & data access</h2><p>PostgreSQL is the active relational database foundation, with EF Core owning application persistence and migrations.</p></div><div class="tech-grid">
            <article class="tech-card"><img src="https://cdn.simpleicons.org/postgresql/4169E1" alt="PostgreSQL logo"/><div><h3>PostgreSQL 16 / 17</h3><p>Primary relational database. PostgreSQL 17 is used by the local Compose environment; PostgreSQL 16 is used in API integration verification.</p><small>Transactional database</small></div></article>
            <article class="tech-card"><img src="https://cdn.simpleicons.org/dotnet/512BD4" alt="Entity Framework logo"/><div><h3>Entity Framework Core 10</h3><p>ORM, tenant-aware persistence, query filters, relational constraints, concurrency handling and versioned database migrations.</p><small>Data access</small></div></article>
            <article class="tech-card"><img src="https://cdn.simpleicons.org/postgresql/4169E1" alt="Npgsql logo"/><div><h3>Npgsql</h3><p>.NET PostgreSQL provider for EF Core and direct database integration; Npgsql OpenTelemetry instrumentation is referenced by the API.</p><small>Database provider & tracing</small></div></article>
            <article class="tech-card"><img src="https://cdn.simpleicons.org/redis/DC382D" alt="Redis logo"/><div><h3>Redis (optional)</h3><p>Optional distributed cache backend supported by CompileCare.Caching HybridCache integration. Not required by the core API deployment.</p><small>Optional cache adapter</small></div></article>
        </div></div>
        <div class="tech-group"><div class="tech-group-heading"><span class="section-kicker">03 / IDENTITY, API & SECURITY</span><h2>Trust, integration contracts & access control</h2><p>Authentication identifies the caller; persisted membership and organization scope determine what that caller may access.</p></div><div class="tech-grid">
            <article class="tech-card"><img src="https://cdn.simpleicons.org/keycloak/4D4D4D" alt="Keycloak logo"/><div><h3>Keycloak 26.2.5</h3><p>Configured local identity provider and realm for development and hosted acceptance. The platform uses standards-based OIDC integration and can be configured against a compatible provider.</p><small>Local identity environment</small></div></article>
            <article class="tech-card"><img src="https://cdn.simpleicons.org/keycloak/4D4D4D" alt="JWT logo"/><div><h3>OIDC & JWT Bearer</h3><p>Issuer, audience, signature, lifetime and subject validation. API authorization derives tenant roles and permission grants from persisted membership.</p><small>Authentication & authorization</small></div></article>
            <article class="tech-card"><img src="https://cdn.simpleicons.org/swagger/85EA2D" alt="OpenAPI logo"/><div><h3>REST & OpenAPI</h3><p>Versioned HTTP/JSON API contracts, with OpenAPI document exposure in Development and explicit endpoint authorization policies.</p><small>API contracts</small></div></article>
            <article class="tech-card"><img src="https://cdn.simpleicons.org/dotnet/512BD4" alt=".NET logo"/><div><h3>CompileCare.ApiClient</h3><p>Reusable .NET named/typed HttpClient registration, tenant/correlation/token handlers, RFC 9457 Problem Details parsing and bounded safe-method resilience.</p><small>Shared integration library</small></div></article>
            <article class="tech-card"><img src="https://cdn.simpleicons.org/nuget/004880" alt="NuGet logo"/><div><h3>NuGet & GitHub Packages</h3><p>Versioned distribution of shared CompileCare packages, with CI package-read permissions and consuming-repository access controls.</p><small>Package distribution</small></div></article>
            <article class="tech-card"><img src="https://cdn.simpleicons.org/dotnet/512BD4" alt=".NET logo"/><div><h3>Microsoft.Extensions.Http.Resilience</h3><p>Timeout, concurrency limiting, circuit breaker and bounded retries for safe HTTP methods; unsafe commands are not automatically replayed.</p><small>Outbound HTTP resilience</small></div></article>
        </div></div>
        <div class="tech-group"><div class="tech-group-heading"><span class="section-kicker">04 / OBSERVABILITY</span><h2>Logs, metrics, traces & health</h2><p>Shared instrumentation supports operational diagnosis while avoiding patient information and secrets in telemetry.</p></div><div class="tech-grid">
            <article class="tech-card"><img src="https://cdn.simpleicons.org/opentelemetry/F5A800" alt="OpenTelemetry logo"/><div><h3>OpenTelemetry 1.15</h3><p>Distributed tracing, metrics and instrumentation for ASP.NET Core, HTTP, runtime, process and database activity.</p><small>Instrumentation standard</small></div></article>
            <article class="tech-card"><img src="https://cdn.simpleicons.org/opentelemetry/F5A800" alt="OpenTelemetry Collector logo"/><div><h3>OpenTelemetry Collector 0.165</h3><p>Local telemetry receiver and pipeline for OTLP data and Prometheus metric export.</p><small>Telemetry pipeline</small></div></article>
            <article class="tech-card"><img src="https://cdn.simpleicons.org/dotnet/512BD4" alt="Serilog logo"/><div><h3>Serilog 4.3</h3><p>Structured application logging with console and Elasticsearch sinks, environment enrichment and exception details.</p><small>Structured logs</small></div></article>
            <article class="tech-card"><img src="https://cdn.simpleicons.org/prometheus/E6522C" alt="Prometheus logo"/><div><h3>Prometheus 3.16</h3><p>Metrics scraping and querying, including application metrics exposed through the telemetry pipeline.</p><small>Metrics backend</small></div></article>
            <article class="tech-card"><img src="https://cdn.simpleicons.org/jaeger/60D0E4" alt="Jaeger logo"/><div><h3>Jaeger 2.23</h3><p>Distributed trace storage and UI for inspecting service requests and database spans in the local stack.</p><small>Trace backend</small></div></article>
            <article class="tech-card"><img src="https://cdn.simpleicons.org/elasticsearch/005571" alt="Elasticsearch logo"/><div><h3>Elasticsearch 8.13</h3><p>Search and storage backend configured for structured application logs in the local observability environment.</p><small>Log storage</small></div></article>
            <article class="tech-card"><img src="https://cdn.simpleicons.org/kibana/E8478B" alt="Kibana logo"/><div><h3>Kibana 8.13</h3><p>Log discovery and visualization, including a provisioned CompileCare log data view in the local stack.</p><small>Log exploration</small></div></article>
            <article class="tech-card"><img src="https://cdn.simpleicons.org/dotnet/512BD4" alt="Health checks logo"/><div><h3>Health & readiness checks</h3><p>Shared health-check extensions and separate liveness/readiness endpoints for runtime and dependency checks.</p><small>Service health</small></div></article>
        </div></div>
        <div class="tech-group"><div class="tech-group-heading"><span class="section-kicker">05 / INFRASTRUCTURE & DELIVERY</span><h2>Containers, automation & runtime edge</h2><p>Repository workflows build, test and verify the platform components in repeatable environments.</p></div><div class="tech-grid">
            <article class="tech-card"><img src="https://cdn.simpleicons.org/docker/2496ED" alt="Docker logo"/><div><h3>Docker</h3><p>Container images for API, Web and test environments, with health checks and isolated integration-test dependencies.</p><small>Container runtime</small></div></article>
            <article class="tech-card"><img src="https://cdn.simpleicons.org/docker/2496ED" alt="Docker Compose logo"/><div><h3>Docker Compose</h3><p>Local orchestration of API, Web, PostgreSQL, Keycloak and the five-service observability stack.</p><small>Local development & CI</small></div></article>
            <article class="tech-card"><img src="https://cdn.simpleicons.org/githubactions/2088FF" alt="GitHub Actions logo"/><div><h3>GitHub Actions</h3><p>Pull-request and push workflows for restore, build, tests, EF model-drift checks, Docker integration verification and local-stack acceptance.</p><small>CI automation</small></div></article>
            <article class="tech-card"><img src="https://cdn.simpleicons.org/nginx/009639" alt="Nginx logo"/><div><h3>Nginx 1.27</h3><p>Static Web container serving the compiled React workspace, with runtime Content Security Policy configuration and validation.</p><small>Web edge container</small></div></article>
            <article class="tech-card"><img src="https://cdn.simpleicons.org/github/181717" alt="GitHub logo"/><div><h3>GitHub repositories</h3><p>Source control, pull-request review, repository permissions, package access and delivery documentation across the CompileCare organization.</p><small>Engineering collaboration</small></div></article>
            <article class="tech-card"><img src="https://cdn.simpleicons.org/dotnet/512BD4" alt=".NET logo"/><div><h3>EF Core CLI & migration scripts</h3><p>Versioned schema changes, model snapshot validation, idempotent SQL generation and reviewed migration release workflow.</p><small>Database lifecycle</small></div></article>
            <article class="tech-card"><img src="https://cdn.simpleicons.org/python/3776AB" alt="Python logo"/><div><h3>Python 3</h3><p>Local development automation for idempotent Keycloak realm/client reconciliation and hosted acceptance tooling.</p><small>Infrastructure automation</small></div></article>
            <article class="tech-card"><img src="https://cdn.simpleicons.org/gnubash/4EAA25" alt="Bash logo"/><div><h3>Bash & Windows Batch</h3><p>Cross-platform local environment launchers, stack verification, cleanup and operational scripts for macOS/Linux and Windows.</p><small>Developer tooling</small></div></article>
            <article class="tech-card"><img src="https://cdn.simpleicons.org/githubcli/2088FF" alt="GitHub CLI logo"/><div><h3>GitHub CLI</h3><p>Local setup tooling uses authenticated GitHub CLI access to retrieve private package-feed credentials without embedding credentials in images.</p><small>Developer tooling</small></div></article>
        </div></div>
        <div class="tech-group"><div class="tech-group-heading"><span class="section-kicker">06 / QUALITY ENGINEERING</span><h2>Automated verification & test tooling</h2><p>Unit, component, browser and database-backed tests are used at different layers.</p></div><div class="tech-grid">
            <article class="tech-card"><img src="https://cdn.simpleicons.org/dotnet/512BD4" alt="xUnit logo"/><div><h3>xUnit</h3><p>.NET unit and PostgreSQL-backed integration test framework for API, security, data and shared-library behavior.</p><small>Backend tests</small></div></article>
            <article class="tech-card"><img src="https://cdn.simpleicons.org/vitest/6E9F18" alt="Vitest logo"/><div><h3>Vitest 5</h3><p>Fast frontend unit and component test runner for the React/TypeScript application.</p><small>Web unit tests</small></div></article>
            <article class="tech-card"><img src="https://cdn.simpleicons.org/testinglibrary/E33332" alt="Testing Library logo"/><div><h3>React Testing Library</h3><p>Component behavior tests focused on user-visible interactions and accessibility semantics.</p><small>Web component tests</small></div></article>
            <article class="tech-card"><img src="https://cdn.simpleicons.org/playwright/2EAD33" alt="Playwright logo"/><div><h3>Playwright 1.65</h3><p>Browser end-to-end checks, including real Keycloak Authorization Code + PKCE flows in isolated hosted acceptance environments.</p><small>Browser E2E</small></div></article>
            <article class="tech-card"><img src="https://cdn.simpleicons.org/postgresql/4169E1" alt="PostgreSQL logo"/><div><h3>PostgreSQL integration fixtures</h3><p>Disposable database tests apply migrations and verify tenant isolation, concurrency, audit behavior and no-mutation guarantees.</p><small>Database integration</small></div></article>
        </div></div>
        <div class="tech-group"><div class="tech-group-heading"><span class="section-kicker">07 / DIRECT LIBRARIES & PACKAGE TOOLING</span><h2>Supporting packages and runtime libraries</h2><p>Additional direct dependencies declared in the repositories, grouped by the role they play in the platform.</p></div><div class="tech-grid">
            <article class="tech-card"><img src="https://cdn.simpleicons.org/dotnet/512BD4" alt=".NET logo"/><div><h3>ASP.NET Core & API packages</h3><p>Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authentication.JwtBearer 10.0.0; Microsoft.AspNetCore.OpenApi 10.0.0; Microsoft.OpenApi 2.7.5; Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc.Testing 10.0.0.</p><small>Authentication · API description · test host</small></div></article>
            <article class="tech-card"><img src="https://cdn.simpleicons.org/dotnet/512BD4" alt=".NET logo"/><div><h3>EF Core & PostgreSQL packages</h3><p>Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore 10.0.0; Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Design 10.0.0; Npgsql.EntityFrameworkCore.PostgreSQL 10.0.0; Npgsql.OpenTelemetry 10.0.3.</p><small>ORM · migrations · provider tracing</small></div></article>
            <article class="tech-card"><img src="https://cdn.simpleicons.org/dotnet/512BD4" alt=".NET logo"/><div><h3>HTTP client & resilience packages</h3><p>Microsoft.Extensions.Http 10.0.13; Microsoft.Extensions.Options 10.0.13; Microsoft.Extensions.Http.Resilience 10.11.1.</p><small>Typed clients · configuration · safe-method resilience</small></div></article>
            <article class="tech-card"><img src="https://cdn.simpleicons.org/redis/DC382D" alt="Redis logo"/><div><h3>Hybrid cache packages</h3><p>Microsoft.Extensions.Caching.Hybrid 10.11.0; Microsoft.Extensions.Caching.StackExchangeRedis 10.0.15; Microsoft.Extensions.Configuration and Options 10.0.15.</p><small>Shared cache package · Redis adapter optional</small></div></article>
            <article class="tech-card"><img src="https://cdn.simpleicons.org/opentelemetry/F5A800" alt="OpenTelemetry logo"/><div><h3>OpenTelemetry instrumentations</h3><p>OpenTelemetry API/OTLP 1.15.3; ASP.NET Core, HTTP, Runtime and SqlClient instrumentation 1.12.0; Process instrumentation 1.12.0-beta.1; Prometheus ASP.NET Core exporter 1.12.0-beta.1.</p><small>Tracing · metrics · exporter</small></div></article>
            <article class="tech-card"><img src="https://cdn.simpleicons.org/dotnet/512BD4" alt="Structured logging logo"/><div><h3>Serilog enrichers & sinks</h3><p>Serilog 4.3.0; Serilog.AspNetCore 9.0.0; Environment enricher 3.0.1; Exceptions 8.4.0; Console sink 6.0.0; Elasticsearch sink 10.0.0.</p><small>Structured logging dependencies</small></div></article>
            <article class="tech-card"><img src="https://cdn.simpleicons.org/vitest/6E9F18" alt="Vitest logo"/><div><h3>Frontend build & test packages</h3><p>@@vitejs/plugin-react 5.0.4; TypeScript 5.9.3; Vitest 5.1.1; jsdom 27.0.0; @@testing-library/react 16.3.0; jest-dom 6.9.1.</p><small>Browser-like component test environment</small></div></article>
            <article class="tech-card"><img src="https://cdn.simpleicons.org/dotnet/512BD4" alt="xUnit logo"/><div><h3>.NET test packages</h3><p>Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk 17.14.1; xUnit 2.9.3; xunit.runner.visualstudio 3.1.5; ASP.NET Core MVC Testing 10.0.0.</p><small>Unit · integration · in-memory host</small></div></article>
            <article class="tech-card"><img src="https://cdn.simpleicons.org/githubactions/2088FF" alt="GitHub Actions logo"/><div><h3>CI action toolchain</h3><p>GitHub Actions workflows use checkout v4, setup-dotnet v4 and setup-node v4; the Web CI runtime currently uses Node 22.23.5 and npm 10.9.9.</p><small>Hosted build and verification</small></div></article>
        </div></div>
        <div class="notice"><b>Standards and integrations on the roadmap</b><p>ABDM/ABHA, FHIR, HL7 and DICOM are planned integration standards, not technologies currently represented as connected production integrations. Their implementation requires validated use cases, partner agreements, applicable approvals and conformance/security testing.</p></div>
        <div class="notice notice-bottom"><b>Architecture note</b><p>CompileCare is currently structured as a modular monolith with explicit API, Application and Infrastructure boundaries. The longer-term architecture is extensible, but independent microservices will be introduced only when scale, ownership, deployment or resilience needs justify them. Technology logos identify tools configured in the repositories; they are not endorsements or a claim that every future module is already deployed.</p></div>
    </div></section>
</main>
